# The native backend (stage 2; docs/architecture.md, "Stage 2"): `sisu
# build --native` and `sisu run --native`.
D0103 cli     native.unsupported          the native backend does not compile {what} yet (in `{function}`); `sisu run` without `--native` runs the program
D0104 cli     native.no-runtime           the native runtime `libsisu_rt.a` is not beside `sisu` (in `{dir}`); `cargo build` in `compiler/` builds it
D0105 cli     native.link-failed          linking `{output}` failed: {detail}
D0106 cli     native.built                built `{output}`
D0107 cli     native.internal             internal error in the native backend: {detail}
D0108 cli     native.cannot-run           cannot run `{path}`: {reason}
D0109 cli     native.alone                `--native` builds a native executable and runs it; it does not combine with `{option}`
# `sisu build --from-sir FILE` without `--native` (decisions 212 and 254):
# `sisu run --from-sir FILE` interprets the program.
D0110 cli     native.from-sir             `sisu build --from-sir FILE` compiles a serialised SIR program with the native backend; it goes with `--native`, and `sisu run --from-sir FILE` interprets it
# `--release` without `--native` (decision 232): the profiles are the native
# backend's.
D0111 cli     native.release              `--release` builds with the native backend's release profile (09); it goes with `--native`
# `--features NAMES` on the command line (09, decision 250): a name that is
# not a feature of the package it names.
D0112 cli     cli.unknown-feature         `--features` names `{name}`, which is not a feature of `{package}`; a package's features are the keys of its `[features]`
# `sisu doc --std MODULE...` (decision 258) with a path that names no
# module of the standard library.
D0113 cli     doc.std-path                `{path}` is not a module of the standard library; `sisu doc --std` takes the paths an import names them by, as `std.time`
# `sisu doc` on a program with errors (decision 258): nothing is written.
D0114 cli     doc.errors-found            the documentation was not written: errors found ({count})
# The front end a command uses (decision 268): `--front-end=NAME` or
# `SISU_FRONT_END`, stage 1 by default; its executable, built when a source
# of stage 1 is newer; and stage 1 stopping as no compiler may.
D0115 cli     cli.bad-front-end           `--front-end` takes `stage1` (the front end written in Sisu, the default) or `rust` (the Rust front end, the oracle), not `{value}`
D0116 cli     front.no-stage1             the stage-1 front end is not in `{dir}`; `--front-end=rust` uses the Rust front end
D0117 cli     front.stage1-build          building the stage-1 front end in `{dir}` failed; `--front-end=rust` uses the Rust front end:\n{detail}
D0118 cli     front.stage1-failed         internal compiler error: the stage-1 front end stopped with status {status}; `--front-end=rust` uses the Rust front end
# `--from-lir FILE` without `--native` (decision 284): LIR, the low IR
# stage 2 writes, is compiled by the native backend; nothing interprets it.
D0119 cli     native.from-lir             `--from-lir FILE` builds a LIR program (what stage 2's `sisu2 lir` writes) with the native backend; it goes with `--native`
# How a native build lowers SIR (decision 304): through stage 2, the backend
# written in Sisu, by default, or `--lower=rust` (`SISU_LOWER=rust`) through
# the Rust lowering, the oracle; stage 2's executable, built when a source of
# it is newer; and stage 2 stopping other than on a construct it does not
# lower yet.
D0120 cli     cli.bad-lower               `--lower` takes `stage2` (the lowering written in Sisu, the default) or `rust` (the Rust lowering, the oracle), not `{value}`
D0121 cli     native.stage2-build         building stage 2 in `{dir}` failed; `--lower=rust` lowers with the Rust backend:\n{detail}
D0122 cli     native.stage2-failed        internal compiler error: stage 2 failed to lower the program (status {status}); `--lower=rust` lowers with the Rust backend:\n{detail}
# Which backend compiles LIR to machine code (decisions 306 and 331): the
# x86-64 backend written in Sisu (`sisu2 x86`), the debug profile's default,
# which compiles stage 2's LIR and so not the Rust lowering's, or Cranelift
# through the Rust translation, the release profile's default and the
# oracle (`--backend=NAME`, `SISU_BACKEND=NAME`); and the Sisu backend
# stopping other than on a construct it does not compile yet.
D0123 cli     cli.bad-backend             `--backend` takes `sisu` (the x86-64 backend written in Sisu, the debug profile's default) or `cranelift` (the Rust backend, the release profile's default and the oracle), not `{value}`
D0124 cli     native.backend-lowering     `--backend=sisu` compiles the LIR stage 2 lowers, so it does not go with `--lower=rust`
D0125 cli     native.sisu-failed          internal compiler error: the Sisu backend failed to compile the program (status {status}); `--backend=cranelift` compiles it with the Rust backend:\n{detail}
# The runtime in Sisu (decision 336): compiled once from its seed, the SIR
# stage 1 printed of `compiler/rt`, into the object every native program is
# linked with.
D0126 cli     native.rt-build             building the runtime in Sisu from `{seed}` failed:\n{detail}
# `--explore N` (decision 356): a seed whose run exits as the first's did
# but prints other output differs from it too.
D0127 cli     cli.explore-differs         schedule seed {seed} of {count} printed other output than seed {first}, with the same exit status {status}; `--schedule-seed {seed}` runs it again
